        {
            "number": 7,
            "revision": "b73890679f2da6a2997a2049bda399d29fcabd69",
            "parents": [
                "66403fd2c18fac53edd095a43aca88864bbe2431"
            ],
            "ref": "refs/changes/61/84561/7",
            "uploader": {
                "name": "Souvik Roy",
                "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                "username": "souvik1914581"
            },
            "createdOn": 1761142807,
            "author": {
                "name": "Souvik Roy",
                "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                "username": "souvik1914581"
            },
            "kind": "REWORK",
            "comments": [
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/worker.hpp",
                    "line": 65,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "Why new constructor? Why not modify the same one anyways the value is being defaulted."
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/worker.hpp",
                    "line": 65,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "Souvik Roy",
                        "email": "souvikroyofficial10@gmail.com",
                        "username": "souvik1914581"
                    },
                    "message": "I added a new constructor to avoid changes in the way `worker` is initialized in non-IBM code here https://github.com/openbmc/openpower-vpd-parser/blob/c4fa618189bc05dde54b59d490bf9e83c2513c20/vpd-manager/src/manager.cpp#L149\n\nand also at https://github.com/openbmc/openpower-vpd-parser/blob/c4fa618189bc05dde54b59d490bf9e83c2513c20/vpd-manager/oem-handler/ibm_handler.cpp#L37\n\nwe want to initialize `worker` with default number of threads by using the implicit value for `i_maxThreadCount`. If we change existing `worker` constructor, to `Worker(std::string pathToConfigJson = std::string(),\n           uint8_t i_maxThreadCount = constants::MAX_THREADS, types::VpdCollectionMode i_vpdCollectionMode)`, we cannot initialize `worker` with default number of threads while specifying `i_vpdCollectionMode`"
                },
                {
                    "file": "vpd-manager/include/worker.hpp",
                    "line": 65,
                    "reviewer": {
                        "name": "SunnySrivastava",
                        "email": "sunnsr25@in.ibm.com",
                        "username": "SunnySrivastava1984"
                    },
                    "message": "hmm fair, but there can be other combinations as well to look into.\nLike even by having this constructor we cannot initialize worker with only different collection mode and custom threads.\n\nWhy not keep it simple, either use default value or pass value for all."
